{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Install TanStack Charts and its Octane peer:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"pnpm add @tanstack/charts octane","lang":"sh"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The shared "},{"type":"link","href":"../../concepts/scales-and-d3.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Scales"}]},{"type":"text","value":" page explains the\ncompact scale families and when a chart needs D3 instead."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"define-and-render-a-chart","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Define and render a chart"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Definitions are framework-independent and can be shared with any adapter:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"live-example","tagName":"md-live-example","attributes":{"id":"octane-quick-start-1"},"properties":{"data-example-group":"octane-quick-start","data-collapsed-indexes":"[1]","data-workspace":"{\"version\":1,\"entry\":\"/src/App.tsrx\",\"environment\":\"charts-octane\",\"files\":{\"/src/App.tsrx\":\"import { scaleBand } from '@tanstack/charts/scales/band'\\nimport { scaleLinear } from '@tanstack/charts/scales/linear'\\nimport { barY, defineChart } from '@tanstack/charts'\\nimport { tooltip } from '@tanstack/charts/tooltip'\\nimport { Chart } from '@tanstack/charts/octane'\\nimport { alphabet } from './data'\\n\\nconst percent = new Intl.NumberFormat('en-US', {\\n  style: 'percent',\\n  maximumFractionDigits: 1,\\n})\\n\\nconst letterFrequencyChart = defineChart({\\n  marks: [\\n    barY(alphabet, {\\n      x: 'letter',\\n      y: 'frequency',\\n    }),\\n  ],\\n  scales: {\\n    x: {\\n      scale: () => scaleBand().padding(0.18),\\n    },\\n    y: {\\n      scale: scaleLinear,\\n      nice: true,\\n      grid: true,\\n      axis: {\\n        label: 'Frequency',\\n        ticks: { format: (value) => percent.format(value) },\\n      },\\n    },\\n  },\\n\\n  tooltip,\\n})\\n\\nexport default function App() {\\n  return (\\n    <Chart\\n      definition={letterFrequencyChart}\\n      height={320}\\n      ariaLabel=\\\"English letter frequencies\\\"\\n    />\\n  )\\n}\",\"/src/data.ts\":\"export interface AlphabetRow {\\n  letter: string\\n  frequency: number\\n}\\n\\nexport const alphabet: readonly AlphabetRow[] = [\\n  { letter: 'E', frequency: 0.12702 },\\n  { letter: 'T', frequency: 0.09056 },\\n  { letter: 'A', frequency: 0.08167 },\\n  { letter: 'O', frequency: 0.07507 },\\n  { letter: 'I', frequency: 0.06966 },\\n]\"}}"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"import { scaleBand } from '@tanstack/charts/scales/band'\nimport { scaleLinear } from '@tanstack/charts/scales/linear'\nimport { barY, defineChart } from '@tanstack/charts'\nimport { tooltip } from '@tanstack/charts/tooltip'\nimport { Chart } from '@tanstack/charts/octane'\nimport { alphabet } from './data'\n\nconst percent = new Intl.NumberFormat('en-US', {\n  style: 'percent',\n  maximumFractionDigits: 1,\n})\n\nconst letterFrequencyChart = defineChart({\n  marks: [\n    barY(alphabet, {\n      x: 'letter',\n      y: 'frequency',\n    }),\n  ],\n  scales: {\n    x: {\n      scale: () => scaleBand().padding(0.18),\n    },\n    y: {\n      scale: scaleLinear,\n      nice: true,\n      grid: true,\n      axis: {\n        label: 'Frequency',\n        ticks: { format: (value) => percent.format(value) },\n      },\n    },\n  },\n\n  tooltip,\n})\n\nexport default function App() {\n  return (\n    <Chart\n      definition={letterFrequencyChart}\n      height={320}\n      ariaLabel=\"English letter frequencies\"\n    />\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx","meta":"group=octane-quick-start env=charts-octane file=/src/App.tsrx entry","title":"/src/App.tsrx","file":"/src/App.tsrx"},{"type":"code","value":"export interface AlphabetRow {\n  letter: string\n  frequency: number\n}\n\nexport const alphabet: readonly AlphabetRow[] = [\n  { letter: 'E', frequency: 0.12702 },\n  { letter: 'T', frequency: 0.09056 },\n  { letter: 'A', frequency: 0.08167 },\n  { letter: 'O', frequency: 0.07507 },\n  { letter: 'I', frequency: 0.06966 },\n]","lang":"ts","meta":"group=octane-quick-start file=/src/data.ts collapsed","title":"/src/data.ts","file":"/src/data.ts"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The definition infers the row, scale, and callback types. Normal TSRX authoring\ndoes not need "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Chart"},{"type":"text","value":" generics or casts."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"responsive-sizing","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Responsive sizing"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"height"},{"type":"text","value":" for a fixed-height responsive chart:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<Chart\n  definition={letterFrequencyChart}\n  height={320}\n  ariaLabel=\"English letter frequencies\"\n/>","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"aspectRatio"},{"type":"text","value":" when height should follow width:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<Chart\n  definition={letterFrequencyChart}\n  aspectRatio={16 / 9}\n  initialWidth={720}\n  ariaLabel=\"English letter frequencies\"\n/>","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The server scene uses "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"initialWidth"},{"type":"text","value":", then the shared host measures the actual\ncontainer after hydration. See\n"},{"type":"link","href":"./adapter.md#sizing-and-layout","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Octane adapter"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"memoize-live-definitions","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Memoize live definitions"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { useMemo } from 'octane'\n\ninterface LetterFrequencyInput {\n  rows: readonly AlphabetRow[]\n  accent: string\n}\n\nexport function LiveLetterFrequency({ rows, accent }: LetterFrequencyInput) {\n  const definition = useMemo(() => {\n    return defineChart({\n      marks: [\n        barY(rows, {\n          x: 'letter',\n          y: 'frequency',\n          fill: accent,\n        }),\n      ],\n      scales: {\n        x: {\n          scale: () => scaleBand().padding(0.18),\n        },\n        y: {\n          scale: scaleLinear,\n          nice: true,\n        },\n      },\n\n      svgAnimation: true,\n      tooltip,\n    })\n  })\n\n  return (\n    <Chart\n      definition={definition}\n      height={320}\n      ariaLabel=\"Filtered English letter frequencies\"\n    />\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Octane tracks the values read by "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useMemo"},{"type":"text","value":". Definition identity tells the chart\nhost when captured values changed. See\n"},{"type":"link","href":"../../reference/chart-definitions.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Chart Definition API"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"interaction-callbacks","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Interaction callbacks"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<Chart\n  definition={letterFrequencyChart}\n  height={320}\n  ariaLabel=\"English letter frequencies\"\n  onFocusChange={(point) => {\n    if (point) {\n      console.log(point.datum.letter, point.yValue)\n    }\n  }}\n  onSelect={(point) => {\n    if (point) openLetter(point.datum.letter)\n  }}\n/>","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Grouped focus, tooltip formatting, keyboard behavior, and application-owned\ninteraction are documented in\n"},{"type":"link","href":"../../reference/focus-and-interaction.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Focus and interaction"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Continue with the "},{"type":"link","href":"./adapter.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Octane adapter"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for lifecycle and SSR, the\n"},{"type":"link","href":"./reference/chart.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Chart"},{"type":"text","value":" reference"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for every prop, or the\n"},{"type":"link","href":"../../reference/index.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"core API reference"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"define-and-render-a-chart","text":"Define and render a chart","level":2},{"id":"responsive-sizing","text":"Responsive sizing","level":2},{"id":"memoize-live-definitions","text":"Memoize live definitions","level":2},{"id":"interaction-callbacks","text":"Interaction callbacks","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nInstall TanStack Charts and its Octane peer:\n\n```sh\npnpm add @tanstack/charts octane\n```\n\nThe shared [Scales](../../concepts/scales-and-d3.md) page explains the\ncompact scale families and when a chart needs D3 instead.\n\n## Define and render a chart\n\nDefinitions are framework-independent and can be shared with any adapter:\n\n```tsx group=octane-quick-start env=charts-octane file=/src/App.tsrx entry\nimport { scaleBand } from '@tanstack/charts/scales/band'\nimport { scaleLinear } from '@tanstack/charts/scales/linear'\nimport { barY, defineChart } from '@tanstack/charts'\nimport { tooltip } from '@tanstack/charts/tooltip'\nimport { Chart } from '@tanstack/charts/octane'\nimport { alphabet } from './data'\n\nconst percent = new Intl.NumberFormat('en-US', {\n  style: 'percent',\n  maximumFractionDigits: 1,\n})\n\nconst letterFrequencyChart = defineChart({\n  marks: [\n    barY(alphabet, {\n      x: 'letter',\n      y: 'frequency',\n    }),\n  ],\n  scales: {\n    x: {\n      scale: () => scaleBand().padding(0.18),\n    },\n    y: {\n      scale: scaleLinear,\n      nice: true,\n      grid: true,\n      axis: {\n        label: 'Frequency',\n        ticks: { format: (value) => percent.format(value) },\n      },\n    },\n  },\n\n  tooltip,\n})\n\nexport default function App() {\n  return (\n    <Chart\n      definition={letterFrequencyChart}\n      height={320}\n      ariaLabel=\"English letter frequencies\"\n    />\n  )\n}\n```\n\n```ts group=octane-quick-start file=/src/data.ts collapsed\nexport interface AlphabetRow {\n  letter: string\n  frequency: number\n}\n\nexport const alphabet: readonly AlphabetRow[] = [\n  { letter: 'E', frequency: 0.12702 },\n  { letter: 'T', frequency: 0.09056 },\n  { letter: 'A', frequency: 0.08167 },\n  { letter: 'O', frequency: 0.07507 },\n  { letter: 'I', frequency: 0.06966 },\n]\n```\n\nThe definition infers the row, scale, and callback types. Normal TSRX authoring\ndoes not need `Chart` generics or casts.\n\n## Responsive sizing\n\nUse `height` for a fixed-height responsive chart:\n\n```tsx\n<Chart\n  definition={letterFrequencyChart}\n  height={320}\n  ariaLabel=\"English letter frequencies\"\n/>\n```\n\nUse `aspectRatio` when height should follow width:\n\n```tsx\n<Chart\n  definition={letterFrequencyChart}\n  aspectRatio={16 / 9}\n  initialWidth={720}\n  ariaLabel=\"English letter frequencies\"\n/>\n```\n\nThe server scene uses `initialWidth`, then the shared host measures the actual\ncontainer after hydration. See\n[Octane adapter](./adapter.md#sizing-and-layout).\n\n## Memoize live definitions\n\n```tsx\nimport { useMemo } from 'octane'\n\ninterface LetterFrequencyInput {\n  rows: readonly AlphabetRow[]\n  accent: string\n}\n\nexport function LiveLetterFrequency({ rows, accent }: LetterFrequencyInput) {\n  const definition = useMemo(() => {\n    return defineChart({\n      marks: [\n        barY(rows, {\n          x: 'letter',\n          y: 'frequency',\n          fill: accent,\n        }),\n      ],\n      scales: {\n        x: {\n          scale: () => scaleBand().padding(0.18),\n        },\n        y: {\n          scale: scaleLinear,\n          nice: true,\n        },\n      },\n\n      svgAnimation: true,\n      tooltip,\n    })\n  })\n\n  return (\n    <Chart\n      definition={definition}\n      height={320}\n      ariaLabel=\"Filtered English letter frequencies\"\n    />\n  )\n}\n```\n\nOctane tracks the values read by `useMemo`. Definition identity tells the chart\nhost when captured values changed. See\n[Chart Definition API](../../reference/chart-definitions.md).\n\n## Interaction callbacks\n\n```tsx\n<Chart\n  definition={letterFrequencyChart}\n  height={320}\n  ariaLabel=\"English letter frequencies\"\n  onFocusChange={(point) => {\n    if (point) {\n      console.log(point.datum.letter, point.yValue)\n    }\n  }}\n  onSelect={(point) => {\n    if (point) openLetter(point.datum.letter)\n  }}\n/>\n```\n\nGrouped focus, tooltip formatting, keyboard behavior, and application-owned\ninteraction are documented in\n[Focus and interaction](../../reference/focus-and-interaction.md).\n\nContinue with the [Octane adapter](./adapter.md) for lifecycle and SSR, the\n[`Chart` reference](./reference/chart.md) for every prop, or the\n[core API reference](../../reference/index.md).\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Octane Quick Start\ndescription: Install the Octane adapter, define a typed chart, render responsive SSR-safe SVG, and add native interaction.\n---\n\nInstall TanStack Charts and its Octane peer:\n\n```sh\npnpm add @tanstack/charts octane\n```\n\nThe shared [Scales](../../concepts/scales-and-d3.md) page explains the\ncompact scale families and when a chart needs D3 instead.\n\n## Define and render a chart\n\nDefinitions are framework-independent and can be shared with any adapter:\n\n```tsx group=octane-quick-start env=charts-octane file=/src/App.tsrx entry\nimport { scaleBand } from '@tanstack/charts/scales/band'\nimport { scaleLinear } from '@tanstack/charts/scales/linear'\nimport { barY, defineChart } from '@tanstack/charts'\nimport { tooltip } from '@tanstack/charts/tooltip'\nimport { Chart } from '@tanstack/charts/octane'\nimport { alphabet } from './data'\n\nconst percent = new Intl.NumberFormat('en-US', {\n  style: 'percent',\n  maximumFractionDigits: 1,\n})\n\nconst letterFrequencyChart = defineChart({\n  marks: [\n    barY(alphabet, {\n      x: 'letter',\n      y: 'frequency',\n    }),\n  ],\n  scales: {\n    x: {\n      scale: () => scaleBand().padding(0.18),\n    },\n    y: {\n      scale: scaleLinear,\n      nice: true,\n      grid: true,\n      axis: {\n        label: 'Frequency',\n        ticks: { format: (value) => percent.format(value) },\n      },\n    },\n  },\n\n  tooltip,\n})\n\nexport default function App() {\n  return (\n    <Chart\n      definition={letterFrequencyChart}\n      height={320}\n      ariaLabel=\"English letter frequencies\"\n    />\n  )\n}\n```\n\n```ts group=octane-quick-start file=/src/data.ts collapsed\nexport interface AlphabetRow {\n  letter: string\n  frequency: number\n}\n\nexport const alphabet: readonly AlphabetRow[] = [\n  { letter: 'E', frequency: 0.12702 },\n  { letter: 'T', frequency: 0.09056 },\n  { letter: 'A', frequency: 0.08167 },\n  { letter: 'O', frequency: 0.07507 },\n  { letter: 'I', frequency: 0.06966 },\n]\n```\n\nThe definition infers the row, scale, and callback types. Normal TSRX authoring\ndoes not need `Chart` generics or casts.\n\n## Responsive sizing\n\nUse `height` for a fixed-height responsive chart:\n\n```tsx\n<Chart\n  definition={letterFrequencyChart}\n  height={320}\n  ariaLabel=\"English letter frequencies\"\n/>\n```\n\nUse `aspectRatio` when height should follow width:\n\n```tsx\n<Chart\n  definition={letterFrequencyChart}\n  aspectRatio={16 / 9}\n  initialWidth={720}\n  ariaLabel=\"English letter frequencies\"\n/>\n```\n\nThe server scene uses `initialWidth`, then the shared host measures the actual\ncontainer after hydration. See\n[Octane adapter](./adapter.md#sizing-and-layout).\n\n## Memoize live definitions\n\n```tsx\nimport { useMemo } from 'octane'\n\ninterface LetterFrequencyInput {\n  rows: readonly AlphabetRow[]\n  accent: string\n}\n\nexport function LiveLetterFrequency({ rows, accent }: LetterFrequencyInput) {\n  const definition = useMemo(() => {\n    return defineChart({\n      marks: [\n        barY(rows, {\n          x: 'letter',\n          y: 'frequency',\n          fill: accent,\n        }),\n      ],\n      scales: {\n        x: {\n          scale: () => scaleBand().padding(0.18),\n        },\n        y: {\n          scale: scaleLinear,\n          nice: true,\n        },\n      },\n\n      svgAnimation: true,\n      tooltip,\n    })\n  })\n\n  return (\n    <Chart\n      definition={definition}\n      height={320}\n      ariaLabel=\"Filtered English letter frequencies\"\n    />\n  )\n}\n```\n\nOctane tracks the values read by `useMemo`. Definition identity tells the chart\nhost when captured values changed. See\n[Chart Definition API](../../reference/chart-definitions.md).\n\n## Interaction callbacks\n\n```tsx\n<Chart\n  definition={letterFrequencyChart}\n  height={320}\n  ariaLabel=\"English letter frequencies\"\n  onFocusChange={(point) => {\n    if (point) {\n      console.log(point.datum.letter, point.yValue)\n    }\n  }}\n  onSelect={(point) => {\n    if (point) openLetter(point.datum.letter)\n  }}\n/>\n```\n\nGrouped focus, tooltip formatting, keyboard behavior, and application-owned\ninteraction are documented in\n[Focus and interaction](../../reference/focus-and-interaction.md).\n\nContinue with the [Octane adapter](./adapter.md) for lifecycle and SSR, the\n[`Chart` reference](./reference/chart.md) for every prop, or the\n[core API reference](../../reference/index.md).\n"}
